  { p: 'Which Tibetan school governed central Tibet in the 13th century, with Mongol support?', op: ['Gelug', 'Sakya', 'Nyingma', 'Bön'], certa: 1, exp: 'The Sakya, with Sakya Pandita and Phagpa, held power, in connection with Godan and Kublai Khan.' },
  { p: 'Who founded the Gelug school and the monastery of Ganden in 1409?', op: ['Milarepa', 'Sakya Pandita', 'Tsongkhapa', 'Songtsen Gampo'], certa: 2, exp: 'Tsongkhapa (1357–1419) founded the school of “the virtuous”, that of the Dalai Lamas.' },
  { p: 'Who granted the title “Dalai Lama” to Sonam Gyatso in 1578?', op: ['Altan Khan', 'Kublai Khan', 'Genghis Khan', 'The Qing emperor'], certa: 0, exp: 'The Mongol Altan Khan gave the title (dalai, “ocean”, in Mongolian) to the third Dalai Lama.' },
  { p: 'Which Portuguese Jesuit reached Tsaparang, in western Tibet, in 1624?', op: ['Francis Xavier', 'António de Andrade', 'Matteo Ricci', 'Ippolito Desideri'], certa: 1, exp: 'António de Andrade was among the first Europeans to describe Tibet. Desideri was Italian and arrived in 1716.' },
  { p: 'Which palace was rebuilt from 1645 under the Fifth Dalai Lama?', op: ['Norbulingka', 'Yumbulakhang', 'Potala', 'Jokhang'], certa: 2, exp: 'The White Palace of the Potala was ready in 1648 and the Red Palace in 1694.' },
  { p: 'About relations between Tibet and China in the Yuan dynasty, what is correct to say?', op: ['All historians agree on its meaning', 'There is agreement on the facts, but different readings of their political meaning', 'There are no sources', 'Tibet never had contact with the Yuan'], certa: 1, exp: 'The facts (Sakya, the Xuanzheng Yuan) are known; the interpretation varies between Chinese, Tibetan and Western historiography.' }
